WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.440
In four steps you go from chatting

2
00:00:01.440 --> 00:00:03.220
to building agents that work

3
00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:04.760
for you: on your computer,

4
00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.260
in a task queue, and on your

5
00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:07.200
social media.

6
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.760
Most people stop at the chat,

7
00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:10.500
copying and pasting answers.

8
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.260
In this video I show you the whole

9
00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:13.760
path, the four steps,

10
00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:14.400
and at the end,

11
00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:15.380
where to start today,

12
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:16.000
for free.

13
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:17.440
Chat is great for asking questions.

14
00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:19.020
But in chat you're the driver

15
00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:20.120
the whole time:

16
00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.840
ask, copy, paste,

17
00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:23.480
tweak, ask again.

18
00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:24.760
When you close the window,

19
00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:25.720
the work stops.

20
00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.020
An agent is different:

21
00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:28.660
it reads your files,

22
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:31.340
runs tasks, and keeps working while you

23
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:32.340
do something else.

24
00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.820
The shift isn't learning a new

25
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:34.300
model.

26
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.420
It's changing where you work:

27
00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:37.120
from the chat to the system.

28
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.720
Step one: OSWork.

29
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:40.200
From chat to the terminal.

30
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.480
You learn folders,

31
00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:43.940
markdown files, the terminal, and the agent

32
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:45.260
working inside a folder,

33
00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:47.440
with Claude Code or Codex.

34
00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:49.680
It sounds technical, but it's only a few commands.

35
00:00:49.680 --> 00:00:51.100
This is where most people get stuck,

36
00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.540
and this is where everything changes:

37
00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.700
you stop typing answers and start

38
00:00:54.700 --> 00:00:55.800
giving tasks.

39
00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.560
Step two: your Jarvis.

40
00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:59.500
With INTELECTO you build a personal

41
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.240
assistant that talks to you on Telegram,

42
00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:03.440
remembers your conversations, and has the personality

43
00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:04.380
you define.

44
00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:05.740
It runs on your computer,

45
00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:07.380
with a cloud or local model.

46
00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:08.880
You no longer open a website to

47
00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:10.600
chat: the assistant is yours.

48
00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:11.570
Step

49
00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:12.340
three: queues.

50
00:01:12.340 --> 00:01:14.000
An agent does one thing at a time.

51
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.100
A queue lets you send ten requests

52
00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.020
and go to sleep.

53
00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:19.280
inemaccbot is a Telegram bot

54
00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:20.380
with a durable queue:

55
00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.580
it saves every task,

56
00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:22.380
resumes if it crashes,

57
00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:24.200
and stops at a gate when it needs

58
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:25.280
your approval.

59
00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.800
Transcribing, dubbing, explainer videos,

60
00:01:27.800 --> 00:01:30.460
courses, reels: everything becomes a task in the queue.

61
00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:31.400
Step

62
00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.980
four: automating social media.

63
00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.640
The seven-step reel,

64
00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.260
r7e, builds a reel with a hook,

65
00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:39.400
desire, fear, ease,

66
00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:42.000
discovery, benefit, and comment.

67
00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.680
promoavatar makes promo videos with an

68
00:01:44.680 --> 00:01:46.040
avatar for each audience.

69
00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:48.120
And xviral:

70
00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.020
finviral, saudeviral, advviral.

71
00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:51.840
Systems that watch what the biggest players

72
00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:52.820
in the niche have posted,

73
00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.480
separate out the numbers and sources,

74
00:01:54.480 --> 00:01:56.220
and publish on their own every day.

75
00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:57.760
You create the viral channel for your

76
00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:58.140
niche.

77
00:01:58.140 --> 00:01:59.200
The order matters.

78
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:00.140
Without step one,

79
00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:01.460
the others can't stand.

80
00:02:01.460 --> 00:02:03.580
There's no miracle of earning while you

81
00:02:03.580 --> 00:02:05.360
sleep if the system doesn't run properly.

82
00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:06.620
First folders and terminal,

83
00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:07.740
then the assistant,

84
00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:08.580
then the queue,

85
00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.420
and only then social media on autopilot.

86
00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.260
Each step has its own video here

87
00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:12.780
on the channel.

88
00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:13.960
Where to start today:

89
00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:15.040
with step one,

90
00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:16.360
OSWork.

91
00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:18.540
The courses, guides, and projects

92
00:02:18.540 --> 00:02:20.607
for each step are on INEMA dot

93
00:02:20.607 --> 00:02:23.300
CLUB, open and free.

94
00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:24.660
Watch the next video,

95
00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:25.300
leave the chat behind,

96
00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.220
and start building your own agents.
